{"ts":"2026-07-28T10:06:41.297Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"4018c32541da6a6805d5bd7d","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"remove","path":"/metadata/dependencies/7"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/dependencies/6/kind","value":"implements"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/dependencies/6/id","value":"pm-nfrhf0"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-28T10:06:41.297Z"}],"before_hash":"b37e815a27a7cb80be08283f8afce6dd362fb8c4ea33f86e6404eed73516226a","after_hash":"e99b1dbb4e67ac39df81ec95551f18367b6d687ebd3effd48b341ef30fdec766","message":"Removed a redundant blocks row: pm-li2fj5 already declares blocked_by toward this item."}
{"ts":"2026-07-30T17:16:28.821Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"6682b76673432e27b62e2ad8","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-30T17:16:28.821Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-07-30T17:16:28.821Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Structural prerequisite recorded 2026-07-30 (evening). Acceptance criteria are stored and returned as a single semicolon-delimited scalar string, not as a collection. Verified on disk and through the read path: the toon field is one quoted string, pm get returns a string of 756 characters on the item I checked, repeated --ac flags accumulate by joining with a semicolon and a space, and --add-ac rejects a criterion that contains a semicolon because that character is the separator. The largest live example carries 195 criteria in one field.\n\nThat means a criterion has no addressable identity today. It cannot be referenced, it cannot carry a per-criterion state, and it cannot be linked to the test that proves it, because there is nothing to link to. Every one of this item's promises depends on that: a machine-checkable predicate has to attach to something, and a criterion that exists only as a substring of a scalar cannot be an attachment point.\n\nSo the first tranche of this item is a representation change, not a predicate language: criteria become an ordered collection of records with stable identity, each able to carry text, an optional predicate, and a verification state, with the existing semicolon-joined form preserved as the rendered projection so no consumer breaks and no history entry becomes unreadable. The separator restriction disappears as a consequence rather than as a fix, and the current rejection of a semicolon inside a criterion becomes the regression test that proves the representation actually changed.\n\nTwo adjacent facts to reuse rather than rediscover. The validate surface already counts criteria, so a count is derivable from the scalar today and any migration must keep that count identical. And an item with criteria but no linked test is exactly the population this item exists to shrink, which makes the criterion-to-test edge the first useful predicate to ship once identity exists."}]}],"before_hash":"e99b1dbb4e67ac39df81ec95551f18367b6d687ebd3effd48b341ef30fdec766","after_hash":"321461fcf9215eed7181715b15609d18e8f32f48352244611865f51f5cc158f5"}
{"ts":"2026-08-02T21:11:33.983Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"5e676b30ed4e8585ecf5ff9e","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-02T21:11:33.983Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Merge consequence of the joined-scalar encoding (2026-08-02). Because acceptance_criteria is one '; '-joined string it is absent from ITEM_UNION_COLLECTION_FIELDS and takes the scalar three-way path, so concurrent --add-ac additions from three branches leave exactly one criterion — the other two survive only as discarded_hash values in the merge receipt. src/core/item/parse.ts:92 documents the opposite ('tag-API parity; disjoint additions merge cleanly across branches'). This is the strongest available argument for giving each criterion an addressable identity: identity is what makes element-wise union possible, so this item's structural fix also removes the loss. Filed as pm-inn5y5 for the immediate defect and the docstring claim."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-02T21:11:33.983Z"}],"before_hash":"321461fcf9215eed7181715b15609d18e8f32f48352244611865f51f5cc158f5","after_hash":"35a2e662dbcac768496c9554030c432fdc6a76bfa39773cd8debd6e395f801ad"}
